---
/**
 * /privacy-first-finance-app
 *
 * Angle: Security-conscious audience. Trust-heavy.
 * Audience: People who won't connect their bank to any app.
 * Intent: "Is there a finance app that actually protects my data?"
 * Keyword cluster: privacy first finance app, encrypted finance app, secure money tracking
 *
 * Narrative: Privacy is not an afterthought — it is the architecture.
 * Every design decision starts with "does this protect the user?"
 */

import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import { pages } from '@/data/pages';
import AngleHero from '@/components/AngleHero.astro';
import Section from '@/components/Section.astro';
import FeatureList from '@/components/FeatureList.astro';
import TrustBadge from '@/components/TrustBadge.astro';
import CTABlock from '@/components/CTABlock.astro';
import SiblingLinks from '@/components/SiblingLinks.astro';

const meta = pages.privacyFirstFinance;
---

<Layout
  title={meta.title}
  description={meta.description}
  canonical={`/${meta.slug}`}
>

  <AngleHero
    title="A Finance App That Never Touches Your Accounts"
    subtitle="AES-256 encrypted. EU-hosted. No bank connections. Your financial data is private — not a product."
    keyword="privacy first finance app"
  />

  <!-- Core argument: Privacy by architecture -->
  <Section
    heading="Privacy is not a feature. It is the foundation."
    bg="stone"
  >
    {/*
      COPY PLACEHOLDER:
      - Most finance apps require bank access — that is a massive attack surface
      - Finzen inverts this: manual entry means zero access to accounts
      - Privacy is baked into the architecture, not bolted on
      - "Your financial data should be as private as your medical data"
    */}
    <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-4">
      <p class="text-base text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">
        When a finance app connects to your bank, it gains access to every transaction, every balance, every account detail. That data becomes a target — for breaches, for advertisers, for data brokers. The more convenient the app, the larger the exposure.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">
        Finzen was built from the ground up with a different philosophy: if the app never accesses your accounts, there is nothing to breach. Manual entry is not just about awareness — it is a security boundary. A deliberate choice to keep your financial life private.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">
        Your financial data is as sensitive as your medical records. It deserves the same level of protection.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- Technical privacy details -->
  <Section heading="The technical details">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <FeatureList
        features={[
          { label: 'AES-256-GCM encryption', detail: 'All data is encrypted client-side before transmission. Symmetric, industry-standard.' },
          { label: 'PBKDF2-SHA256 key derivation', detail: 'Your encryption key is derived from your password. We never store or see it.' },
          { label: 'EU-hosted servers', detail: 'Data stored in the European Union. Subject to GDPR.' },
          { label: 'Zero bank connections', detail: 'No OAuth. No Plaid. No API access to your financial accounts.' },
          { label: 'No data sharing', detail: 'Your data is never sold, shared with advertisers, or used for targeting.' },
          { label: 'No tracking scripts', detail: 'The app does not load third-party trackers or analytics that profile you.' },
        ]}
      />
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- Why manual = private -->
  <Section
    heading="Why manual entry is a privacy feature"
    bg="stone"
  >
    {/*
      COPY PLACEHOLDER:
      - Connect the dots: no bank access = no attack surface
      - You choose what to enter — only relevant data exists
      - The app cannot leak what it never had
      - Reinforces the philosophy: privacy through intentional design
    */}
    <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-4">
      <p class="text-base text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">
        Think about it this way: Finzen can only ever contain the information you choose to put into it. It has never accessed your bank. It does not know your account numbers. It cannot reveal transaction details it never had.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">
        Manual entry is not a limitation — it is a privacy guarantee. You are the gatekeeper. You decide what your financial app knows about you. That is a level of control no auto-syncing app can offer.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <TrustBadge />

  <CTABlock
    heading="Your finances. Your privacy. Your control."
    subtext="No bank connection. No data sharing. Just encrypted, private financial clarity."
  />

  <SiblingLinks slugs={['manualFinanceApp', 'beYourOwnCFO']} />

</Layout>
